# Allowlist, not a denylist.
#
# NOTE ON HOW THIS IS USED: `az acr build` reads .dockerignore from the CONTEXT
# ROOT, not from beside the Dockerfile. Because the context root is the
# repository, this file is NOT consulted during the scripted ACR build.
# aca/deploy.ps1 instead stages a temporary directory containing only the
# allowlisted paths, which is stricter: anything not copied cannot reach the
# image at all.
#
# This file still matters for a local `docker build -f aca/Dockerfile .` run
# from the aca directory, and it documents the intended boundary in one place.
#
# A denylist fails silently: anything a contributor adds later is included by
# default, and the first sign of a mistake is a secret or a local run history
# shipped in a public image. This denies everything, then re-admits only the
# paths the build reads.
#
# Docker evaluates these in order, so every re-admission must come after the
# initial deny, and each directory on a path must be re-admitted before its
# contents can be.

# Deny everything.
**

# Web application source, needed by the node build stage.
!tokenos
!tokenos/apps
!tokenos/apps/web
!tokenos/apps/web/**

# API source, needed by the runtime stage.
!tokenos/services
!tokenos/services/tokenos-api
!tokenos/services/tokenos-api/**

# Re-deny anything that must never reach a hosted image, even though it sits
# under a path allowed above.
tokenos/apps/web/node_modules/**
tokenos/apps/web/dist/**
tokenos/services/tokenos-api/tests/**
tokenos/services/tokenos-api/.venv/**
tokenos/services/tokenos-api/.pytest_cache/**
tokenos/services/tokenos-api/static/**
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.pyc
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-journal
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.bak

# The production image vendors these wheels to install the Foundry extra. The
# judge image must not have the provider SDK available at all, so they are
# excluded from the context rather than merely left uninstalled.
tokenos/vendor-wheels/**
